---
import Research from '../../layouts/Research.astro';
import ImagingPlayer from '../../components/ImagingPlayer.astro';
import CA1Layers from '../../components/CA1Layers.astro';
import Label from '../../components/Label.astro';
---
<Research theme="two-photon" color="var(--green)" eyebrow="Research · 01" title="Two-photon imaging in hippocampal CA1"
  lead="Watching identified neurons in the living hippocampus — cell by cell, day after day.">
  <Fragment slot="question">
    <h2 class="ph">[PLACEHOLDER] The lab’s central question for this theme.</h2>
    <p class="muted">Replace with 2–3 sentences in the lab’s own words, e.g. what CA1 activity patterns the group studies and why they matter.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="method">
    <div class="grid grid-2" style="align-items:center">
      <div>
        <h2>Why two photons?</h2>
        <p>A two-photon microscope uses pulsed infrared light. Fluorescence is only excited where two photons arrive at the same time — practically only in the tiny focal spot. This gives sharp optical sections deep in scattering tissue with less photodamage.</p>
        <p class="muted">With genetically encoded calcium indicators such as GCaMP, neurons light up when they are active, so the activity of hundreds of cells can be followed simultaneously.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="figure">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 400 260" role="img" aria-labelledby="tp-t">
          <title id="tp-t">One-photon excitation produces fluorescence along the whole light cone; two-photon excitation only at the focal point.</title>
          <g font-family="JetBrains Mono Variable, monospace" font-size="11" fill="var(--text-3)">
            <text x="100" y="20" text-anchor="middle">one-photon</text><text x="300" y="20" text-anchor="middle">two-photon</text>
          </g>
          <path d="M60 40 L140 40 L100 150 Z M100 150 L60 250 L140 250 Z" fill="var(--blue)" opacity=".18" />
          <path d="M60 40 L140 40 L100 150 Z M100 150 L60 250 L140 250 Z" fill="var(--green)" opacity=".35" />
          <path d="M260 40 L340 40 L300 150 Z M300 150 L260 250 L340 250 Z" fill="#c0392b" opacity=".18" />
          <circle cx="300" cy="150" r="7" fill="var(--green)" />
          <circle cx="300" cy="150" r="16" fill="var(--green)" opacity=".25" />
        </svg>
        <figcaption><Label kind="schematic" /> <span>Excitation volume (green): one- vs two-photon.</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="data">
    <h2 data-reveal>Explore imaging channels</h2>
    <p class="muted" data-reveal>Toggle channels, adjust their intensity and scrub through time. Indicator, depth, frame rate and scale are shown with every recording.</p>
    <div style="margin-top:var(--s4)"><ImagingPlayer /></div>
    <h3 style="margin-top:var(--s6)">Where we image</h3>
    <CA1Layers />
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="findings">
    <h2 class="ph">[PLACEHOLDER] Key findings</h2>
    <ul class="muted"><li>[Finding 1 — link to paper]</li><li>[Finding 2 — link to paper]</li><li>[Finding 3 — link to paper]</li></ul>
  </Fragment>
</Research>
